{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods","id":135690,"title":"Spirits and Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-13T13:18:27-07:00","id":135690,"title":"Spirits and Gods","content":"So I start running my <b>Werewolf</b> game located in North Sweden. Today I was listening inspirational music and come to me - will in Shadow Realm beings like Viking gods? Characters like Odin, Loki, Thor, Heimdall and all those courts? Are they Spirits in the Shadow? Or maybe ther are more rulers in Astral Realms of humanity? How <b>Forsaken</b> gameline comes to this topic? Obviously we have multiple moon godesses/gods in person of Mother Luna / Father Moon, isn't it? So how about other gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T13:27:27-07:00","id":135713,"title":"","content":"Just about all of the gods from various human cultures solely exist as beings in the Astral, as figments of humanity's belief and imagination. The exceptions to this most likely will be very bizarre and primal deities, which are entities from other worlds that built a cult following. Prehistoric and animist religions heavily featured spirits, but if a god is human-like in appearance, it almost certainly won't be found in the Shadow. A God of the Shadow refers to immensely powerful spirits of world-spanning phenomena, but which aren't different from other spirits - just scaled up. Anthropomorphism is rare in the hisil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T13:39:10-07:00","id":135722,"title":"","content":"Paganism was a very long time ago and I'd think an Odin-like spirit would probably look more like the Christian God nowadays. On the other hand, that's less interesting; you can have Christian spirits practically anywhere, but Odin probably isn't going to be moving much outside Northern Europe.<br /> <br /> On a side note, although it's not a Forsaken book, Summoners for Awakening has Thunderer (or something) a rank 5+ spirit who looks bears a vague resemblance to Thor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T14:50:59-07:00","id":135761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=135713#post135713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just about all of the gods from various human cultures solely exist as beings in the Astral, as figments of humanity's belief and imagination. The exceptions to this most likely will be very bizarre and primal deities, which are entities from other worlds that built a cult following. Prehistoric and animist religions heavily featured spirits, but if a god is human-like in appearance, it almost certainly won't be found in the Shadow. A God of the Shadow refers to immensely powerful spirits of world-spanning phenomena, but which aren't different from other spirits - just scaled up. Anthropomorphism is rare in the hisil.</div> </div> </div> </div> Just because mortals think of a god as being anthropomorphic doesn't mean they're right. Think about a thunder god. Ancient peoples of all sorts of cultures experience the phenomena of thunder and lightning, and to explain it, create a story about this mighty being hurling spears of light from the heavens or something. They made this entity up, but the energy they devote to its warship could easily be consumed by the actual weather spirits responsible, causing them to grow stronger and more akin to the entity the stories speak of. Over time, their belief may become self-fulfilling, turning what was once just a thunder spirit into a highly ranked force of nature just like the stories say. The humans depict this entity as human because it helps them identify with it, but that doesn't mean the spirit that's been growing fat off their worship and playing into their legends to further fuel their belief actually looks that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T14:51:57-07:00","id":135762,"title":"","content":"Honestly, it's whatever you want it to be in your game. There is no hard-and-fast canon. Odin, Thor, Heimdall, and so forth can be represented by spirits, things from the Astral Realm, True Fae...whatever makes for the best story for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:03:24-07:00","id":135770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anthropomorphism is rare in the hisil. </div> </div> </div>That depends on what you count as anthropomorphism. A lot of the picture show spirits that, while obviously not human, have a vaguely human shape to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:05:17-07:00","id":135773,"title":"","content":"I could see some amalgam of Odin and Zeus and some others having formed into an &quot;All Father&quot; kind of figure. Owing to many of the different myths in Europe having been printed and spread and told and taught in schools. Probably comes across as a big, rolling thundercloud that has some vague forms in it like bulls and ravens and such.<br /> <br /> Maybe even the form of a lion or a bear to include some of the more &quot;kingly&quot; symbols from other parts of the region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:13:20-07:00","id":135809,"title":"","content":"It's important to recognize the darwinian aspect of the Shadow and how it interacts with the Gurihal. It doesn't matter what people think, that is the domain of the Astral, it matters what people feel and do. Action and emotion mold the Shadow, concepts and ideas mold the Astral. Somewhere in the Astral is a specific entity called Thor that we would collectively recognize as the Norse Thunder God of legend. There might be many thunder spirits of sufficient power and rank that resemble Thor, the Thunderer is a great example, but there's no hard/fast way of knowing if it was the original spirit that inspired the legends of Thor or if being recognized as such is a survival advantage and some lesser thunder spirit just rose through the ranks in that form. It's left intentionally ambiguous.<br /> <br /> There's a little excerpt in Imperial Mysteries that might help clear up a few things. Spirits of nations or huge swaths of the earth (such as oceans) and phenomenon such as thunder or drought are generally rank 6 and amongst spirits counted as Lesser Gods. Spirits of whole species and global events are counted as Gods and count the Firstborn among their ranks. Spirits of cosmic power are rank 8 and the only two known spirits of this rank are Luna and Helios. There's a theoretical spirit of Gaia that's rank 9, but nobody has been able to confirm that such an entity exists at all. This is all assuming that you take Imperial Mysteries as canon since it does mess with the original spirit ranking system in Forsaken to make room for the Primal Wilds as the Rank 10 spirit of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:53:33-07:00","id":135841,"title":"","content":"Odds are the gods we know of have four to seven incarnations, maybe more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T17:11:50-07:00","id":135889,"title":"","content":"I would pick certain gods and make them the Firstborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T17:27:41-07:00","id":135932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=135809#post135809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter what people think, that is the domain of the Astral, it matters what people feel and do. Action and emotion mold the Shadow, concepts and ideas mold the Astral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite true. I can't tell you what the Astral has, but the Shadow has conceptual and ideological spirits. There are spirits in the ideological choir that specifically encompass human concepts that are not emotionally related, such as &quot;duty,&quot; &quot;teachery,&quot; &quot;midnight,&quot; &quot;silence,&quot; and so forth. Part of the whole point of powerful spirits is that they have influences based upon the ideas of humans. Snakes can have influences of wisdom and betrayal, fertility and life, solely based on the ideas of man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=135713#post135713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prehistoric and animist religions heavily featured spirits, but if a god is human-like in appearance, it almost certainly won't be found in the Shadow. A God of the Shadow refers to immensely powerful spirits of world-spanning phenomena, but which aren't different from other spirits - just scaled up. Anthropomorphism is rare in the hisil.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there are plenty of anthropomorphic spirits. The totem of the Lodge of the Shadow Throne claims to be a shade of King Solomon, while exhibiting aspects of a spirit of rulership, one of the totems available for Elodoths is Blind Justice (a blind woman with her bands bound and scales on her back). Generally, the more powerful a spirit is, the more likely it is to have multiple forms, but spirits of any rank may be anthropomorphic. Predators mentions anthropomorphic kudzu-spirits.<br /> <br /> Gods would certainly fit in the Shadow, though the more significant the being the more likely they'd be unreachable by the average werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-13-2014, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:11:42-07:00","id":136265,"title":"","content":"All posts are great, I thanks all of you for your contribution. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=135773#post135773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see some amalgam of Odin and Zeus and some others having formed into an &quot;All Father&quot; kind of figure. Owing to many of the different myths in Europe having been printed and spread and told and taught in schools. Probably comes across as a big, rolling thundercloud that has some vague forms in it like bulls and ravens and such.<br /> <br /> Maybe even the form of a lion or a bear to include some of the more &quot;kingly&quot; symbols from other parts of the region.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same I thought. But with more antropocentric figure - old man, with towering presence, with accompany of crows ( for Scandinavia ). All Father would be based on <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dyeus\" target=\"_blank\">Dyeus</a> of Proto-Indo-European pantheon, and would probably have Influences of Creation (???) and Wisdom. Ban would be very tricky, as we put together many beings for it, but maybe &quot;You must rule of all others&quot;, to the position of knowing head god of it's pantheons. Also important wuestion is about his Rank - would he be Rank 6, Rank 7 or Rank 8 spirit?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:17:03-07:00","id":136268,"title":"","content":"A point of note: There is a great, grand,origin point Stag spirit and a great, grand, origin point Snake spirit.<br /> <br /> The Aeons for Life and Spirit are Stag and Snake.<br /> <br /> No One really knows if the Aeons and these Incarnae are different beings. They might be, might not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:18:27-07:00","id":136269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=135809#post135809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a little excerpt in Imperial Mysteries that might help clear up a few things. Spirits of nations or huge swaths of the earth (such as oceans) and phenomenon such as thunder or drought are generally rank 6 and amongst spirits counted as Lesser Gods. Spirits of whole species and global events are counted as Gods and count the Firstborn among their ranks. Spirits of cosmic power are rank 8 and the only two known spirits of this rank are Luna and Helios. There's a theoretical spirit of Gaia that's rank 9, but nobody has been able to confirm that such an entity exists at all. This is all assuming that you take Imperial Mysteries as canon since it does mess with the original spirit ranking system in Forsaken to make room for the Primal Wilds as the Rank 10 spirit of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>So chief spirits of pantheons could be Rank 7, where typical gods would be placed on Rank 6?<br /> <br /> Other question - could werewolf pack take for example All Father or Thunderer as they Totem? If not, maybe entity loyal to them, like Lunes are working for Luna?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:21:02-07:00","id":136273,"title":"","content":"My question is what rank is the spirit of Europa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:24:50-07:00","id":136278,"title":"","content":"It's funny how all the major Incarna that dominate the UK are characters from William Blake's mythology - Urizen, Enitharmon, Orc, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:27:17-07:00","id":136280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=136273#post136273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is what rank is the spirit of Europa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 7, probably? European are they own species. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It would also make logical inclination that Gaia is Rank 9. One continent is two Ranks lower compared to whole planet, and then two spirits of Land and Water. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T23:18:35-07:00","id":136340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=136269#post136269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other question - could werewolf pack take for example All Father or Thunderer as they Totem? If not, maybe entity loyal to them, like Lunes are working for Luna?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally the Pure go after big totems like that, but I think in this case, although they're not revered as much as they once were, their repute has probably kept them from deteriorating too much (even if it has twisted them to become media friendly). They'd probably be too powerful for a pack, and a pack would probably be enslaved by the sheer force of their will if they deigned to become totems for individual wolves.<br /> <br /> Minions, on the other hand, sure. A valkyrie, rune stone spirits, a lightning or storm spirit (these two are probably in Predators book), stuff like that would fit fine. For some reason I think there's a Lodge that has Odin's ravens as totems (or his wolves) but I'm tired and sick so who knows.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T02:33:24-07:00","id":136423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=136269#post136269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So chief spirits of pantheons could be Rank 7, where typical gods would be placed on Rank 6?<br /> <br /> Other question - could werewolf pack take for example All Father or Thunderer as they Totem? If not, maybe entity loyal to them, like Lunes are working for Luna?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, those spirits could be patrons of a whole tribe. They wouldn't be set with a meager pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T06:45:58-07:00","id":136625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=136423#post136423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, those spirits could be patrons of a whole tribe. They wouldn't be set with a meager pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>BUT...... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> All-Father-Thunder might not be available as a pack totem, but a lesser member of his court, say &quot;The Crash Before The Storm&quot; (maybe a Gaffling, looks like a crow made of wind and thunder) would be. And that would be a nice way to get All-Father-Thunder to at least listen when the pack needs help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T08:03:10-07:00","id":136711,"title":"","content":"<b>Papa Bear</b>, could write All-Father-Thunder and The-Crash-Before-Storm up? What Influencas and Rank would they have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-14-2014, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:37:21-07:00","id":136808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=136711#post136711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Papa Bear</b>, could write All-Father-Thunder and The-Crash-Before-Storm up? What Influencas and Rank would they have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting into the crunch is one of my weak areas, but here's what I can give right now.<br /> <br /> I think All-Father-Thunder would have to be pushed up to a Rank 7. He\u2019s going to be the spirit created by all those feelings and thoughts and actions based on an all-powerful, father-like figure from the sky. That means he\u2019s going to have aspects of Odin, Zeus, Ra, YHVH, etc, etc, etc. This figure is all over the place in Europe, which makes it insanely powerful. Major Influences would be things like lightning and thunder, clouds and wind, wisdom and justice, authority and law. This is also the spirit of all those high kings and divinely allowed overlords of the universe. I think it would appear as either a lion or a bull, and it\u2019s kind of hard to tell sometimes because he\u2019s surrounded with rumbling thunder and dark clouds, especially when angry\u2026.which is often the reason he appears. When he\u2019s coming in a gentler aspect, there would be a light shining thru the clouds as if from above. He can be the aspect of authority as a punisher and as a protector, but he\u2019s rarely subtle or light-trodding.<br /> <br /> The Crash Before The Storm is one of his harbingers. A little storm crow made up of that buzzing in the air before a storm. The wind that brings the smell of ozone to let you know what\u2019s coming. Probably no more than a Greater Gaffling (Rank 2), might make it to Lesser Jaggling while attached to a pack. Influences would be wind and sounds (low thunder in the background), a little bit of premonition based on fore-shadowing and warning signs, speed and flight (since it always has to stay ahead of the storm)\u2026.no more than 2 dots in each. Numina \u2013 Blast, Chorus, Reaching (for little blasts of air), Wilds Sense (so it knows where All-Father-Thunder is at all times). Higher Finesse and Resistance than Power. This little guy isn\u2019t about power, it\u2019s about warning people about the in-coming power!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 05-14-2014, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T13:34:23-07:00","id":137112,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot, I maybe use them in my coming chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I would to point out that I'm only starting to familiarize myself with all spirits rules in <b>Forsaken</b>.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=136808#post136808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would appear as either a lion or a bull, and it\u2019s kind of hard to tell sometimes because he\u2019s surrounded with rumbling thunder and dark clouds, especially when angry\u2026.which is often the reason he appears. When he\u2019s coming in a gentler aspect, there would be a light shining thru the clouds as if from above. He can be the aspect of authority as a punisher and as a protector, but he\u2019s rarely subtle or light-trodding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get those forms as alternatives. But shouldn't he also appear as towering male statue clouded by storm clouds? Like, you know, FATHER-Thunder?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=136808#post136808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably no more than a Greater Gaffling (Rank 2), might make it to Lesser Jaggling while attached to a pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a spirit becoming totem can rise in Rank?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=136808#post136808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Influences would be wind and sounds (low thunder in the background), a little bit of premonition based on fore-shadowing and warning signs, speed and flight (since it always has to stay ahead of the storm)\u2026.no more than 2 dots in each.</div> </div> </div> </div>So spirit can have mutiple Influances up to his Rank? So Rank 2 spirit can have four Influnaces on 2 - like Wind 2, Sound 2, Premoniton 2 and Flight 1?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T14:29:42-07:00","id":137163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=137112#post137112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get those forms as alternatives. But shouldn't he also appear as towering male statue clouded by storm clouds? Like, you know, FATHER-Thunder?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but keep in mind that this is the Shadow Realm.<br /> <br /> First, there are no human spirits in the Shadow. Humanoid, sure, but not human. They'll rarely be anything but a vague resemblance to a human form, if they ever come close.<br /> <br /> Second, before even Zeus and Odin, bear-kings and lion-lords were roaming the Shadow and any spirits of fatherly authority and law-bringing were probably gobbled up by them. That they were tied to a sky/cloud ideal doesn't matter as much as they were &quot;high-father&quot; enough for them. It just means they expanded their authority from the ground to the sky. And the Shadow has a long, long, <i>long </i>memory. The feelings about something have to be gone for a very long time before it fades completely from the Shadow. Most of the Black Forest is probably still in tact in the Shadow, if due to no other reason than the reputation it's gained thru folklore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=137112#post137112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a spirit becoming totem can rise in Rank?<br /> <br /> So spirit can have mutiple Influances up to his Rank? So Rank 2 spirit can have four Influnaces on 2 - like Wind 2, Sound 2, Premoniton 2 and Flight 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>Double check the corebook's spirit rules, but if I remember correctly, yes to both, though I'm pretty sure The Clash Before The Storm wouldn't have more than maybe one or two Influences where All-Father-Thunder would have a host of them.<br /> <br /> And just <i>becoming </i>a Pack Totem wouldn't raise the Rank of the spirit, but if the pack prospers, the spirit will have a steady diet and opportunities to grow, allowing it to increase in Rank after a fashion.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, I apologize for some shorter answers, I'm pressed for time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 05-14-2014, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T14:51:45-07:00","id":137214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=136273#post136273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is what rank is the spirit of Europa.</div> </div> </div> </div> Conceptual or Locational?<br /> <br /> Conceptual I'd say rather low. Probably a Rank below most of the national Conceptual Spirits. Most people think more about their nation than Europe itself.<br /> <br /> Geological, 8 for sure. Gaia is 9 so one down from that. I disagree about Land and Water; they're conceptual Spirits. A Geological spirit like Europa would have a continuous border (including parts of the sea, certainly everything between the mainland, UK, and Scandinavia to the north. Spain and Italy to the south, etc) while Land and Water do not.<br /> <br /> Note that this doesn't quite match Shadows of the UK (the only book I know of with an actual rank for a spirit of the land). But since the implication puts Jerusalem and the Man Under London at the same rank; and Jerusalem is the spirit of all cities in the UK while the Man Under London is definitely something subordinate to London itself so probably two ranks down. (The Man Under London most probably isn't the Spirit of London, since the probably City Father is mentioned lower down as a Lodge Patron)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, my view is simple. Most classic Gods such as Zeus, Odin, Jesus, etc are part of the Empyrean mentioned in WoD Inferno. However a God is so massive that it creates Rank 5+ Spirits by it's mere existence.<br /> <br /> Keyword is most. Sometimes it's a spirit that's big enough to create Empyrean beings as it's shadow. And of course there's the Deathlords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T06:32:58-07:00","id":139246,"title":"","content":"Mmm? The Norse Gods you say? I've actually been thinking a bit about this before, and I think I've come up with a rather good solution.<br /> <br /> The gods, the Aesir an Vanir. Oh they are out there. Just not... In the guise one would expect from reading the myths. They are composite beings, let's take the All-father for instance.<br /> <br /> At his core is a spirit, let us call it Glad-of-War, which after all was one of the All-father's kennings (official nicknames, kinda). Glad-of-war is a spirit of death and war. It enjoys it when people wage war, and sometimes it helps people to victory, sometimes he hobbles an army, allowing it to be ground down to dog-meat. Glad-of-war has a theme of wolves and ravens, because those were important death-symbols to the old Norse. It wouldn't surprise me if Glad-of-War is the patron to a particularly savage Bone Shadow Lodge. In fact, it would surprise me if it wasn't. Glad-of-War can be seen as a hooded figure riding a monstrous wolf, and trailing behind him are scores of lesser death spirits, in the forms of shades of warriors, ravens and wolves. He always finds battle, and there he feasts on death.<br /> <br /> That is one facet of him, that mortals have seen and rightfully feared. Another is the Terrible One (Yggr, which means Terrible one in Old Norse, another of Odin's Kennings). A magnificent fae lord who rides out on his eight-legged steed that can run from one world to the next. He wields an unstoppable spear and is followed by bloodthirsty maidens riding giant wolves with crow wings. He is one of the leaders of the Wild Hunt, and he is someone you should fear.<br /> <br /> Grimnir (means masked in old Norse) was a sorcerer who came from across the Baltic Sea from Finland or Russia, no one is really sure. He was a cruel and clever man who set up rulership of a large region of Sweden around the ancient cities of H\u00e5tuna and Uppsala. He ruled all with an iron fist, and threw down the old order. How he died no one is sure, but his memory got woven into myth all the same.<br /> <br /> Many of the Avernian Gates of Northern Europe leads to an enormous field in each end of which is an enormous hall. Each day, legions of ghosts storm from each of them. One is commanded by Draugadrottin (The Lord of the Undead, yet another of Odin's names...) while the other is ruled by an enigmatic queen known only as The Lady (Or if we want to use Old Norse, Freyja.) Each of these two death lords send out ghosts in the shapes of terrible women hunting for great warriors, that they can slay and drag down to fight for their rulers until the end of days.<br /> <br /> And Finally, the Seers of the Throne manipulated these views to fit with their idea of the Father. The great and terrible ruler of all mankind.<br /> <br /> All these, who are relatively similar were seen by men to be one god. And they named him the All-father, and refused to speak his name in case he heard it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Freyja is a mighty sorceress. Similar in origin to Odin. Only with a theme of cats instead of wolves and ravens. And a lot more sex.<br /> She was a Fey in origin, under the title of Vanadis (The Queen of the Vanir, and who ruled the bright elves of Alfheim).<br /> She was the mythic Necromancer-queen of Jylland, whose soldiers were denied rest, and was unbeatable in battle, so men murdered her at night.<br /> She is the greatest of the Valkyires, minor goddesses of death that haunt the Astral Realms, drawing strength from all who died because of a broken clasp in the armour, or a bullet that went astray.<br /> She is, as mentioned, a rival death lord, sitting in her hall across from the Lord of the Undead, gathering her own Einherjaren.<br /> She is the memory of an Ochema sent down by the Psychopomp, to make sure that no one forgot that they would die. Their souls belong to It, not anything else.<br /> <br /> Thor is kinda similar.<br /> He was a spirit of storms. Those terrible thunderstorms that happens when the hot air of the Russian Summer comes crashing into the cold air of the North Sea.<br /> He was a great warrior, wielding a crude sledge-hammer against the evil things that came crawling out from the dark trying to eat humans. Perhaps a Werewolf? No one remembers, because this was myth in the age of Vikings.<br /> He was the astral personification of refusal to stand down to great challenges. A hall full of giants? Do not move. Age herself? Do not move. The Serpent that encircles the world? Do. Not. Move.<br /> He was the General. The Exarch of Forces sending his image down to the people. A great warrior wielding the forces of nature to destroy his enemies.<br /> <br /> Ran is probably one of the simpler. She merely is a spirit that hungers for everything that moves on the surface of the sea, and calls her daughters, the storms, to fetch it down for her. Alas, the dream of feasting with her at the bottom of the sea is probably a myth. She is also probably one of the stronger beings around, being the spirit of the North Sea.<br /> <br /> Hel is simple, just as Ran. The angry, half-dead Death Lord (lady?) that rules her realm of shadows (Ok, originally Helheim wasn't THAT bad, but it got mixed up with the Christian ideas of hell), and this land lies beyond the river of adder-poison in the Underworld. Not deadly, but damnably painful.<br /> <br /> I also think Loki is fairly simple as well. He is one of the more &quot;human&quot; of the gods. I'd rule him the memory of a Changeling who travelled the Northern Lands. Always ready with a quick reply and a backhanded comment, but never truly evil. His Mask wasn't perfect, so people could see that there was something wrong with his mouth \u2014 something he explained with how the dark elves once had sewn his mouth shut with unbreakable thread, so he had to tear it out. He could also take different shapes, and could conjure fire. Both easily within reach of a normal Changeling. In fact, I think Loki (Which means liar, by the way) was one of the sources for the myths about the Norse Pantheon to begin with, as he liked to travel and tell stories. He was a Skald, simple as that. Either Spring or Autumn Court. Or perhaps a now forgotten Court that was common in Scandinavia in the 5th and 6th centuries. Alas, poor Loki was found by his Keeper, and dragged deep underground and chained with entrails, to sit there and wait forever. Or, perhaps, that was just a story he told would happen when he got caught. Perhaps he is still out here?<br /> <br /> Perhaps a lot of Mage here, but if we look at the source material it makes sense. But this was my two cents. I hope you enjoyed reading it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":585,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","user":"Seidmadr","date":". 05-16-2014, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T07:06:32-07:00","id":139275,"title":"","content":"I love your handling of the pantheon; that's a nice, complex origin which befuddled various beings (which I'm a big fan of), and you seem to know the source material very well. I'm booking marking this to use later. Very nice job, Seidmadr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T07:22:26-07:00","id":139304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=139275#post139275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love your handling of the pantheon; that's a nice, complex origin which befuddled various beings (which I'm a big fan of), and you seem to know the source material very well. I'm booking marking this to use later. Very nice job, Seidmadr.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! That's exactly the feedback that makes me happy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I really should've written out Freyja's and Thor's descriptions more, but I don't really know any Kennings for them. :P<br /> Could google it, I suppose..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T07:32:59-07:00","id":139311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=137214#post137214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Geological, 8 for sure. Gaia is 9 so one down from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>One down from Gaia is Luna and Helios.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T18:43:03-07:00","id":151906,"title":"","content":"Crossover question: I've been running More then Human rules in my games of late and one origin that is particularly popular is that of the Demigod, a mortal (supernatural) being with one human and onen divine parent. If I were to incorporate these spirit-gods into the scenery, and I would love to, how could these powerful spirits, locked away in the Shadow by their own power, create fleshly offspring?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I ask for so little. Just fear me, <b>love me</b>, do as I say and I will be your slave.<br /> -Jareth, Goblin King","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2846-jhornb02","name":"jhornb02","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2846_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T18:57:02-07:00","id":151929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jhornb02</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=151906#post151906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossover question: I've been running More then Human rules in my games of late and one origin that is particularly popular is that of the Demigod, a mortal (supernatural) being with one human and onen divine parent. If I were to incorporate these spirit-gods into the scenery, and I would love to, how could these powerful spirits, locked away in the Shadow by their own power, create fleshly offspring?</div> </div> </div> </div>Create Influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T03:31:18-07:00","id":152302,"title":"","content":"Or sent a Royal Avatar (a Rank 5 spirit representing some aspect of the bigger god-self).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T07:17:10-07:00","id":152480,"title":"","content":"The mortal can always wander thru a Locus and end up in the Shadow for a bit. Just long enough for some nookie, then the Shadow god's court escorts them back out again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T12:35:30-07:00","id":152800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=152480#post152480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mortal can always wander thru a Locus and end up in the Shadow for a bit. Just long enough for some nookie, then the Shadow god's court escorts them back out again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Side question on this - I want my ex-Bale Hound mentor to open Shadow Realm for Wolf-Blooded players so they could make they Rite of Passage by hunting they pack totem. How she could make it? Using official rules it would be 5th dot Rite and I don't think she could have it - she is &quot;only&quot; manipulating Irraka.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T12:49:04-07:00","id":152825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=139311#post139311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One down from Gaia is Luna and Helios.</div> </div> </div> </div>No reason why there can't be more at that Rank. It makes sense that the geological spirits form an unbroken chain of Ranks with Gaia at the top.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T13:08:39-07:00","id":152884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=152800#post152800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side question on this - I want my ex-Bale Hound mentor to open Shadow Realm for Wolf-Blooded players so they could make they Rite of Passage by hunting they pack totem. How she could make it? Using official rules it would be 5th dot Rite and I don't think she could have it - she is &quot;only&quot; manipulating Irraka.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember if there's anything useful in the corebook, but I know Book of Spirits has info about mortals stumbling into the Shadow at Loci and Verges and such. Might be easier for her to find one of those than get that Rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T17:11:08-07:00","id":153263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=152800#post152800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side question on this - I want my ex-Bale Hound mentor to open Shadow Realm for Wolf-Blooded players so they could make they Rite of Passage by hunting they pack totem. How she could make it? Using official rules it would be 5th dot Rite and I don't think she could have it - she is &quot;only&quot; manipulating Irraka.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your werewolf can just take them with him into the Shadow through a Locus. Taking people with you is called Pathfinding and detailed on p. 251 of the rulebook. Summarized, your ex-Bale Hound will have a -3 penalty on the Stepping Sideways roll per Wolf-Blooded he takes with him at the same time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=152825#post152825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No reason why there can't be more at that Rank. It makes sense that the geological spirits form an unbroken chain of Ranks with Gaia at the top.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the only known Rank 8 spirits are Luna and Helios, and there are no known spirits of Rank 9 or higher. The existence of Gaia at Rank 9 is conjecture.<br /> <br /> This could open up room for hidden Rank 8 continent spirits, if the ST wants, but that depends on how his cosmology works. I use an Earth-centric (and human-centric) cosmology, where Gaia's choir does not consist of the spirits of continents, mountains and oceans, but of Luna, Helios and the other planets. The spirits of continents, mountains and oceans at Rank 6 and races of animals at Rank 7 (and of course the even lower earthen spirits) are part of Gaia, just as the lunes are part of Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T23:06:58-07:00","id":153568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=153263#post153263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your werewolf can just take them with him into the Shadow through a Locus. Taking people with you is called Pathfinding and detailed on p. 251 of the rulebook. Summarized, your ex-Bale Hound will have a -3 penalty on the Stepping Sideways roll per Wolf-Blooded he takes with him at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i read it more as -2 modifier, as Wolf-Blooded are for me &quot;spiritual responsive&quot; kind, per corebook.<br /> <br /> But idea is that she opens the passage to Shadow Realm, let them go, and wait on the material side in the Locus, watching on the other side from time to time for them. Would this thing be possible without this 5 Dot Rite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T01:07:38-07:00","id":153598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=153568#post153568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, i read it more as -2 modifier, as Wolf-Blooded are for me &quot;spiritual responsive&quot; kind, per corebook.<br /> <br /> But idea is that she opens the passage to Shadow Realm, let them go, and wait on the material side in the Locus, watching on the other side from time to time for them. Would this thing be possible without this 5 Dot Rite?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I would recommend using a keyed Verge, that opens after performing some kind of simple ritual or sacrifice. More information kan be found on p. 53 of the Book of Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T13:56:50-07:00","id":177316,"title":"","content":"As I return to <b>All-Father-Thunder</b>\u2019s Court idea for our game, I will need a bit help in fleshing couple more spirits NPCs.<br /> <br /> But first, let\u2019s recall what\u2019s being set on idea to this day:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=136808#post136808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <b>All-Father-Thunder</b> would have to be pushed up to a Rank 7. He\u2019s going to be the spirit created by all those feelings and thoughts and actions based on an all-powerful, father- like figure from the sky. That means he\u2019s going to have aspects of Odin, Zeus, Ra, YHVH, etc, etc, etc. This figure is all over the place in Europe, which makes it insanely powerful. Major Influences would be things like lightning and thunder, clouds and wind, wisdom and justice, authority and law. This is also the spirit of all those high kings and divinely allowed overlords of the universe. I think it would appear as either a lion or a bull, and it\u2019s kind of hard to tell sometimes because he\u2019s surrounded with rumbling thunder and dark clouds, especially when angry\u2026.which is often the reason he appears. When he\u2019s coming in a gentler aspect, there would be a light shining thru the clouds as if from above. He can be the aspect of authority as a punisher and as a protector, but he\u2019s rarely subtle or light-trodding.<br /> <br /> The <b>Crash Before The Storm</b> is one of his harbingers. A little storm crow made up of that buzzing in the air before a storm. The wind that brings the smell of ozone to let you know what\u2019s coming. Probably no more than a Greater Gaffling (Rank 2), might make it to Lesser Jaggling while attached to a pack. Influences would be wind and sounds (low thunder in the background), a little bit of premonition based on fore-shadowing and warning signs, speed and flight (since it always has to stay ahead of the storm)\u2026.no more than 2 dots in each. Numina \u2013 Blast, Chorus, Reaching (for little blasts of air), Wilds Sense (so it knows where All-Father-Thunder is at all times). Higher Finesse and Resistance than Power. This little guy isn\u2019t about power, it\u2019s about warning people about the in-coming power!</div> </div> </div> </div>So here are my questions to this idea:<br /> <br /> 1. As <b>All-Father-Thunder</b> is Rank 7 being, he would be outside of regional influence. But local court would be ruled by his Royal Avatar, yes? If so, does Avatar knows about everything what <b>All-Father-Thunde</b>r knows, or only his regional domain? What kind of Ban and Bane would be suitable for entity like this?<br /> <br /> 2. Odin is often depicted in company of two wolves - <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geri_and_Freki\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Geri</b> and <b>Freki</b></a> - so I assume some alliance with Firstborns is in order? With whom of ancient Wolf Gods? Would powerful spirit wolf be part of Court, like Rank 4 or maybe 5? Maybe even this wolf spirit is from linage of one of Firstborns? Because I don\u2019t think so that Firstborn himself would be working for <b>All-Father-Thunder</b>, even if he is Rank 7 entity.<br /> <br /> 3. Odin also is surrounded by <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valkyrie\" target=\"_blank\">Valkyries</a></b> in myths. But are they something that could have spirit analogy in Shadow? If yes, what kind would those spirit be? Death and war humanoids?<br /> <br /> 4. Any more spirits could be populate this court? Probably ravens, lesser wolves, but also wisdom and war spirits? Most probably wisdom spirits would be ravens and wars ones would be wolves? How many spirits should be in this kind of local court? Any other kinds could also?<br /> <br /> 5. Last question - were would local court like this gather in Shadow Realm? In some suitable Locus? I was thinking of ancient tree in middle of forest were in time immemorial people would make sacrifices to All-Father-Thunder thinking he is Odin by strangling humans on the branches of tree.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-22-2014, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T16:07:10-07:00","id":177403,"title":"","content":"1. Not an avatar so much as a servant. As the lunes are to Luna, not part of her, but things that come from her. It wouldn't know everything All-Father-Thunder knew but it would probably get audience with the higher power and feel orders from it. The spirit wouldn't know everything about anything, though with its servant spies it would probably know a lot of its region, particularly the aspects of the spirits that serve it.<br /> <br /> 2. Not all wolves are on the Firstborn's side, and if they are it's not necessarily the Forsaken's side of them. Spirits like these would likely be at the sides of your All-Father-Thunder, and occasionally sent to dig into something or assist AFT's servants (like this choir) in their defense, since AFT wouldn't be likely to come themself. There's descendant spirits of the firstborn who are totems for lodges, it wouldn't be hard to consider them that 'level' of power.<br /> <br /> 3. No matter how anthropomorphic, a spirit will never be human. The human form is just something they wear because it's appropriate for them to do so. All Father Thunderer wouldn't be Odin from the Thor movies, giving words of wisdom, he'd be a force of nature writ large across the skies, sending his message with great booms of thunder and strikes of lightning, and most wouldn't understand the communique.<br /> That out of the way, I'll point you to the Valkyria mot. It's sort of a lodge, and it has valkyries as patron spirits. To quote:<br /> 'Several ancestor-spirits serve as this group's totems, usually given the customary names of Brynhildr, Freja, Goll, Gondul, Gudr, Gunn, Herfjoturr, Hildr, Hladgunnr, Hlokk, Hrist, Sigrdrifa, Sigrun and Svafa' (I left out the accents). 'These spirits are often cold and sometimes demand great sacrifices of their daughters' (the mot is female only).<br /> <br /> 4. Yeah, ravens symbolizing wisdom, wolves symbolizing war is fine, you'll want some weather and elemental spirits old and young. And since the Shadow isn't Disney World, some apathy spirits who get a rush whenever people pass by the holy grounds and dismiss them as a bunch of trees or rocks or whatever.<br /> There'd be a lot of spirits, but it's not like a city where you'd go and see everyone (the river spirit doesn't likely leave the river, but it might send rank 1 spirits in its stead if the choir was doing something important).<br /> <br /> 5. They tend to be around loci, so they can stay fat and fed. If you went with the tree, you'll want to make it a more dark and sinister-feeling place, with death and sacrifice spirits and maybe even a ghost or two stuck in Twilight, anchored to the tree.<br /> You may want it to seem bigger than it is, everythng echoing the legends of the past where crowds would gather and watch. You'd probably have some things there that don't exactly mesh in the real world (fallen trees looking perfectly healthy in the Shadow, scary bodies hanging from ropes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T17:12:20-07:00","id":177465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=177316#post177316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I return to <b>All-Father-Thunder</b>\u2019s Court idea for our game, I will need a bit help in fleshing couple more spirits NPCs.<br /> <br /> But first, let\u2019s recall what\u2019s being set on idea to this day:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So here are my questions to this idea:<br /> <br /> 1. As <b>All-Father-Thunder</b> is Rank 7 being, he would be outside of regional influence. But local court would be ruled by his Royal Avatar, yes? If so, does Avatar knows about everything what <b>All-Father-Thunde</b>r knows, or only his regional domain? What kind of Ban and Bane would be suitable for entity like this?<br /> <br /> 2. Odin is often depicted in company of two wolves - <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geri_and_Freki\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Geri</b> and <b>Freki</b></a> - so I assume some alliance with Firstborns is in order? With whom of ancient Wolf Gods? Would powerful spirit wolf be part of Court, like Rank 4 or maybe 5? Maybe even this wolf spirit is from linage of one of Firstborns? Because I don\u2019t think so that Firstborn himself would be working for <b>All-Father-Thunder</b>, even if he is Rank 7 entity.<br /> <br /> 3. Odin also is surrounded by <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valkyrie\" target=\"_blank\">Valkyries</a></b> in myths. But are they something that could have spirit analogy in Shadow? If yes, what kind would those spirit be? Death and war humanoids?<br /> <br /> 4. Any more spirits could be populate this court? Probably ravens, lesser wolves, but also wisdom and war spirits? Most probably wisdom spirits would be ravens and wars ones would be wolves? How many spirits should be in this kind of local court? Any other kinds could also?<br /> <br /> 5. Last question - were would local court like this gather in Shadow Realm? In some suitable Locus? I was thinking of ancient tree in middle of forest were in time immemorial people would make sacrifices to All-Father-Thunder thinking he is Odin by strangling humans on the branches of tree.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Regarding Odin, he has aspects that are a big part of his presentation, and to make him true to the myths they should all be represented. First off, his missing eye. That one is obvious. He lacks one of his eyes, and that follows him no matter what shape he takes. Secondly, his spear. Gungnir, the magical spear that cannot be stopped by anything short of a command from Odin himself. Third, his servants. Freki and Geri are givens, so is Sleipnir, his horse. Most important though are Huginn and Muninn, who are literally parts of him. They are his thoughts and his memories given shape. All of these need to be present to give shape to the god if one is to be close to his original character.<br /> <br /> Valkyries are most certainly death-spirits. Basically humanoid. They could fly, and this was either via giant wolves with raven wings, or they had those wings themselves. In fact, there are anthropologists who argue that the modern view of angels came from Valkyries, only, you know, with dyed wings.<br /> <br /> The kinds of spirits that populate his court? War, Wisdom, Lies, Strength, and first and foremost, Death. <br /> <br /> As to where he would hold court? Well, I'd say a Place That Isn't. One of those places in the shadow without a representation in the Material, a realm created by the All-Father himself, that might connect to Loci of proper essence, where death-spirits in the guise of emaciated wolves stalk and make sure the essence isn't corrupted. If I were to make this I'd have it be a giant hall, with living trees as walls and pillars, and high overhead would be the shadowy shapes of hanged sacrifices. <br /> <br /> A bonus: From Odin's throne one could see EVERYTHING, in all the nine worlds, one just had to know what to look for to see it. Could be a fun thing to toss into a campaign, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T20:20:18-07:00","id":177589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=177465#post177465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Odin, he has aspects that are a big part of his presentation, and to make him true to the myths they should all be represented. First off, his missing eye. That one is obvious. He lacks one of his eyes, and that follows him no matter what shape he takes. Secondly, his spear. Gungnir, the magical spear that cannot be stopped by anything short of a command from Odin himself. Third, his servants. Freki and Geri are givens, so is Sleipnir, his horse. Most important though are Huginn and Muninn, who are literally parts of him. They are his thoughts and his memories given shape. All of these need to be present to give shape to the god if one is to be close to his original character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that <b>All-Father-Thunder</b> <i>isn't</i> Odin. He is just powerful Elemental spirit, mixed in the ways with Royal and Justice. He is universal being that pretending to be Odin, Zeus and other Dyus Petra dependents. He adapt to local myths and legends, making his regional avatars surrounded by spirits that should reflects mortal stories to even more Essence he should get with they sacrifices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=177465#post177465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Valkyries are most certainly death-spirits. Basically humanoid. They could fly, and this was either via giant wolves with raven wings, or they had those wings themselves. In fact, there are anthropologists who argue that the modern view of angels came from Valkyries, only, you know, with dyed wings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool image, thank you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=177465#post177465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to where he would hold court? Well, I'd say a Place That Isn't. One of those places in the shadow without a representation in the Material, a realm created by the All-Father himself, that might connect to Loci of proper essence, where death-spirits in the guise of emaciated wolves stalk and make sure the essence isn't corrupted. If I were to make this I'd have it be a giant hall, with living trees as walls and pillars, and high overhead would be the shadowy shapes of hanged sacrifices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could agree for the All-Father Thunder himself domain, but not his local avatar for regional game we run. None the less. it will be cool place to visit at the ending of chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=177465#post177465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bonus: From Odin's throne one could see EVERYTHING, in all the nine worlds, one just had to know what to look for to see it. Could be a fun thing to toss into a campaign, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T10:00:36-07:00","id":178040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=177589#post177589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand that <b>All-Father-Thunder</b> <i>isn't</i> Odin. He is just powerful Elemental spirit, mixed in the ways with Royal and Justice. He is universal being that pretending to be Odin, Zeus and other Dyus Petra dependents. He adapt to local myths and legends, making his regional avatars surrounded by spirits that should reflects mortal stories to even more Essence he should get with they sacrifices.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know. I just wanted to drop them in to give you ideas if you wanted to have an Odin-like aspect here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=177589#post177589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could agree for the All-Father Thunder himself domain, but not his local avatar for regional game we run. None the less. it will be cool place to visit at the ending of chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What about a smaller version of this hall, set as a minor domain warding a locus like this? Keeping the path to his realm secure?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":585,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","user":"Seidmadr","date":". 06-23-2014, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T00:34:04-07:00","id":179521,"title":"","content":"So my PCs will need to find a tomb of Dark Ages &quot;hero&quot; of Uratha that fight under patronage of <b>All-Father-Thunder</b>. They need the information of location of tomb, lost millennium ago. What kind of chiminage on meeting and favor for this information our god would required from them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T10:52:04-07:00","id":179860,"title":"","content":"That's the kind of thing that requires a favor in exchange for the knowledge, and the favor being its own little quest of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T12:11:37-07:00","id":179919,"title":"","content":"And it's exaclty as to what I'm asking...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=179521#post179521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my PCs will need to find a tomb of Dark Ages &quot;hero&quot; of Uratha that fight under patronage of <b>All-Father-Thunder</b>. They need the information of location of tomb, lost millennium ago. What kind of chiminage on meeting and favor for this information our god would required from them?</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of payment the All-Father-Thunder demand? What would want this kind powerful elemental-protection-justice spirits? What could players need to done to get All-Father-Thunder's avatar information?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T15:25:50-07:00","id":180121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So my PCs will need to find a tomb of Dark Ages &quot;hero&quot; of Uratha that fight under patronage of <b>All-Father-Thunder</b>. They need the information of location of tomb, lost millennium ago. What kind of chiminage on meeting and favor for this information our god would required from them? </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Cahalith's roar needs to beat His Thunder's decibels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T23:23:48-07:00","id":180470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/135690-spirits-and-gods?p=180121#post180121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Cahalith's roar needs to beat His Thunder's decibels.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really think that &quot;roaring contest&quot; is the best? I would like to engage mostly our Elodoth, as playeress is somehow on sideways in the pack. It's time to make her lead, in some way. But how? She want's to become Storm Lord, so best would be some test of Honor for her also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T01:27:08-07:00","id":180512,"title":"","content":"Well, NOW that we have a little more stipulations... She's not mute, let her be the one to figure out A) The Daddy Thunder loves contests of manly endeavors and B) How to actually allow the Cahalith to win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T06:02:29-07:00","id":180729,"title":"","content":"There is a problem with this approach - when other Auspice have things to do: Itheaur is doing spirit research, Cathalith is making &quot;scenes&quot; and &quot;howls&quot;, and Irraka is doing scouting or planing ambushes. The Elodoth what do? They ask Storyteller for info how other should help him? Nothing to do here for her, it's me telling what she would need...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T07:10:24-07:00","id":180766,"title":"","content":"Hey man, I'm just telling you possible objectives. Up to you to figure out what leaps and bounds she might have to go thru in order to accomplish it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T14:28:36-07:00","id":181241,"title":"","content":"Okay, my Elodoth playeress want be on game session, so her we can take out of chiminage scene. The bigger problem is this - what could All-Father-Thunder would want from PCs for his info? Hanging man for the sacrificial death of him by Air, like &quot;Odin&quot; would like? Or maybe some difficult quest for them? To stole a lighting? Nah, it's probably too big for Uratha. What would Thunder god want from werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T14:36:15-07:00","id":181243,"title":"","content":"How about one of them hanging himself in emulation of Odin?<br /> <br /> The character doesn't has to die, but it's not implied, and it sets the stage for a nice -back to life- moment for the one who hanged himself for knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T14:45:18-07:00","id":181262,"title":"","content":"Would want a more quest-like thing, so players could be busy for second half of session. And finding and hanging other man in sacrifice could be interesting moral problem - will character appease old god by making obvious inhuman act? Also, could use new Harmony mechanics a bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But some a more journey needing alternative is needed also, as probably players will want to slip from moral dilemma situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T23:36:24-08:00","id":398491,"title":"","content":"Analyzing couple of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths\">alternative Uratha myths</a>, with taking in account that Father's/Mother's Wolf and Luna's/Moon's gender is irrelevant, but still they are described in local myths with account on male or female identity - it made come to conclusion that those spirits of Rank 6+ could use Royal Avatars that are more akin to local myths and tales - to suck the Essence from the mortals worship. In that vein Wolf god can be both <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capitoline_Wolf\" target=\"_blank\">Capitoline She-Wolf</a> and Father Wolf of from two difference myths. Death Wolf could walk among humans in female form, to study the end of mortals. So what do you think about this theory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:00:11-08:00","id":399203,"title":"","content":"If remember correctly one of the writers said before that spirits don't have genders at all. It is humanity that labels their gender--or if the spirit decides to pick gender. Even in real life many spiritualist claim and believe that animist spirits don't have genders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}